     * <ul>
     *   <li>disable DTD processing ({@code SUPPORT_DTD = false})</li>
     *   <li>disable resolution of external entities ({@code IS_SUPPORTING_EXTERNAL_ENTITIES = false})</li>
     *   <li>enable coalescing of character data ({@code IS_COALESCING = true})</li>
     *   <li>replace entity references with their replacement text ({@code IS_REPLACING_ENTITY_REFERENCES = true})</li>
     * </ul>
     *
     * <p>If the underlying XML parser implementation does not support any of the security
     * properties, the method fails fast with a clear {@link XMLStreamException} so that the
     * caller can handle the situation appropriately.
     *
     * @param inputStream the raw XML input stream (must not be {@code null})
     * @return a configured {@link XMLStreamReader}
     * @throws XMLStreamException if the XML parser cannot be configured securely or if parsing fails
     * @throws IOException        if an I/O error occurs while wrapping the stream
     */
    private static final XMLStreamReader createXMLStreamReader(InputStream inputStream)
            throws XMLStreamException, IOException {

        if (inputStream == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("InputStream must not be null");
        }

        XMLInputFactory factory = XMLInputFactory.newInstance();

        // Harden the factory against XXE attacks.
        // These properties are defined by the StAX specification; if a particular
        // implementation does not support them, an IllegalArgumentException is thrown.
        // We let the exception propagate as XMLStreamException to make the failure explicit.
        try {
